On 2007-08-13, Henry J Cobb <hcobb@io.com> wrote:
> Since poison is no longer an instant kill for players, why allow a level 
> one rogue or tourist to instant kill most monsters?

1) A tourist must find a potion of sickness before he can poison his darts;
for him to do so before reaching XL2 is nearly impossible.  It may take
a large number of levels, in fact.

2) A rogue must find darts.  This normally only takes wandering a few
levels in the mines until he trips over a trap, but again, to do so before 
reaching XL2 is nearly impossible.

3) Deadly poison is a 10% chance per hit if the monster is not poison
resistant.  This means you could quite easily pump 9 poisoned darts into a
monster without any effect.  (I believe Rogues get a small boost to the
chance of the instakill.  I am still OK with this.)

> Give monsters a fighting chance against poison.

There is no need.

